From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winmm: mixer TARGETTYPE lines, MCI element ids, MIDI patch cache checks, mmio memory file growth

FIXMEs and stubs, as documented now:

- mixerGetLineInfo with MIXER_GETLINEINFOF_TARGETTYPE (FIXME, MIXERR_INVALLINE):
  the destination or source line whose Target is the given device type and
  name (and the device's ids); an unknown target type is MMSYSERR_INVALPARAM.
- mciGetDeviceIDFromElementIDW ("stub", always 0): the open device of that
  type that was opened with MCI_OPEN_ELEMENT_ID and this id.
- midiOutCachePatches / midiOutCacheDrumPatches: the handle, patch array,
  flags and bank/patch are validated; a valid request is
  MMSYSERR_NOTSUPPORTED (the synthesizer loads patches itself). No FIXME.
- mmioWrite on a memory file: a full buffer stops the write, or grows a
  moveable global buffer by the expansion size in adwInfo[0] (it used to wrap
  around and overwrite the start); mmioMemIOProc keeps adwInfo[0] on open.
- joyConfigChanged: success without the FIXME (nothing to reload).

---
diff --git a/dlls/winmm/joystick.c b/dlls/winmm/joystick.c
index 0028b5c..efb72c1 100644
--- a/dlls/winmm/joystick.c
+++ b/dlls/winmm/joystick.c
@@ -355,7 +355,8 @@ static void CALLBACK joystick_timer( HWND hwnd, UINT msg, UINT_PTR timer, DWORD
  */
 MMRESULT WINAPI joyConfigChanged(DWORD flags)
 {
-    FIXME( "flags %#lx stub!\n", flags );
+    TRACE( "flags %#lx\n", flags );
+    /* the configuration is read each time it is needed: there is nothing to reload */
     if (flags) return JOYERR_PARMS;
     return JOYERR_NOERROR;
 }
